<title>BELGIUM: European Commission's Brittan pays tribute to Deng.</title>
<headline>European Commission's Brittan pays tribute to Deng.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sir Leon Brittan, European Commissioner with responsibility for relations with Asia, said he expected China to continue along the path of modernisation set out by paramount leader Deng Xiaoping, whose death was announced on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;Deng played a remarkable and courageous role as leader, sure the leadership he provided will continue for many years to help China to add still further to the outstanding achievements of recent years.&quot;</p>
<p>European Commission President Jacques Santer was not immediately available for comment.</p>
</text>
